- How handle duplicates or dynamic k?  
- What are alternatives (order-statistics tree, Fenwick) and trade-offs?  
- How does complexity change if B ≫ k?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes understanding of streaming frequency estimation with bounded memory, a common real-world requirement in analytics dashboards.

## Key Concepts

- Misra-Gries algorithm for frequent items
- Online/update-time vs. memory trade-offs
- Error bounds and how they scale with N and s

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo
class MG {
  constructor(s){
    this.s = s;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  add(x){
    if (this.counters.has(x)) { this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x)+1); return; }
    if (this.counters.size < this.s-1) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
      return;
    }
    for (let k of Array.from(this.counters.keys())) {
      this.counters.set(k, this.counters.get(k)-1);
      if (this.counters.get(k) === 0) this.counters.delete(k);
    }
  }
  topK(k){
    // return top k by counts
    return [...this.counters.entries()].sort((a,b)=>b[1]-a[1]).slice(0,k);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to choose s for a desired error?
- What if there are ties in top-3?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of space-time trade-offs in streaming analysis. Introduces hashing-based approximation and how it affects accuracy, latency, and memory.

## Key Concepts
- Hash bucketing for compact counts
- Amortized batch updates
- Probability of collision vs. accuracy
- Space-time trade-offs vs. exact counting

## Code Example
```javascript
class BucketCounter {
  constructor(D) {
    this.D = D;
    this.buckets = new Array(D).fill(0);
    this.max = 0;
  }
  updateBatch(batch, hashFn) {
    for (const c of batch) {
      const b = hashFn(c) % this.D;
      this.buckets[b] += 1;
      if (this.buckets[b] > this.max) this.max = this.buckets[b];
    }
  }
  query(t) { return this.max >= t; }
}
```

